      "text": "Fort Cobb was established as a U.S. Army frontier post in Indian Territory on October 1, 1859.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Cobb%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The fort was named after Secretary of the Treasury Howell Cobb, a friend of the founding officer, Major William Emory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Cobb%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lieutenant Colonel George Armstrong Custer's command was encamped at Fort Cobb from December 1868 to January 1869.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
